prop:
Decision: `render --out` also writes a render record, <memo>.tetel/render.json. It holds the sha256 of the document bytes written, a map from each SNAPSHOT_FILES name present in the snapshot to that file's sha256, and buildid::label().

snapshot::write takes over the whole publication from both render --out callers, which pass it the rendered bytes, so neither caller can forget a step or misorder them. In order, it:
1. removes any existing render.json, before the identity mint or anything else that can fail;
2. writes the document;
3. makes the snapshot a mirror: copies each SNAPSHOT_FILES name the workspace has, and removes each one it lacks;
4. writes the new record, only if compose::render over the snapshot directory reproduces the rendered bytes exactly.

The removal comes first, so an interruption or failure at any later step leaves no record. That never reads as DocumentEdited against a record of an older pair. It reads as Unattributed once the document or snapshot has started to change, and as an unrecorded Matches if nothing had changed yet.

The mirror is needed because a file carried forward from an earlier workspace, which the copy-only loop does today, would make a correct render fail its own certification. The certification is needed because rendering and copying are separate reads of the workspace, and without it the record could certify a pair that never matched. If certification fails, the error names the first differing line.
